## Why this directory is licensed separately

Freehold's core — transaction management, CRM, portals, workflows,
integrations, the credential vault, backups, reporting — is complete and
free to self-host under the Elastic License 2.0. Nothing in `ee/` is
required to build, run, or self-host Freehold.

`ee/` contains Freehold Cloud's billing and plan-gating logic: Stripe
checkout, subscription and credit-pack handling, coupon issuance, and
related plan enforcement. This code is published for transparency — so
anyone can see exactly how Freehold Cloud bills and gates plans — not for
reuse in a competing product or service.

## Permitted without a commercial agreement

- Reading, cloning, and inspecting the Software for any purpose.
- Building and running the Software locally for development, testing, and
  evaluation — including running Freehold's own test suite against it.
- Modifying the Software and submitting patches back to Freehold under the
  repository's Contributor License Agreement (see CONTRIBUTING.md).
- Forking the repository, provided any production deployment of a fork
  either omits `ee/` entirely or holds its own commercial agreement as
  described below.

## Requires a commercial agreement

Using the Software, or any modified version of it, in production —
meaning any deployment that serves real users, processes real payments,
or is otherwise relied upon outside of development and testing — requires
a separate, signed commercial agreement with Freehold. Becoming a Freehold
Cloud customer, or otherwise reaching a written agreement with Freehold,
satisfies this requirement for that deployment only.

Absent such an agreement, you may not copy, merge, publish, distribute,
sublicense, sell, host, or offer the Software, or any modified or
derivative version of it, to any third party, whether directly, as part
of a hosted or managed service, or bundled with another product.

